  authorName: Pete van Norman
  publishDate: February 21, 2068
  HeadlineText: Do schools still have all the resources to provide a good study for the students
  detailsText: Schools across the country are facing difficulties due to the ongoing water shortage. Students are no longer allowed to use water for certain school projects and practical experiments.   Teachers are worried that the lack of water will affect the quality of education. Some subjects, such as chemistry, biology, and science, depend on water for experiments and practical lessons.   Schools are now looking for alternative ways to teach students without using too much water.
